  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.3.0.0\n\t\t\t- Audits are now written to the host's ILogger as well as to storage, each output with its own switch under IsAuditEnabled: IsAuditDatabaseLoggingEnabled and IsAuditAppInsightsLoggingEnabled. Both default to true.\n\t\t\t- WARNING: because IsAuditAppInsightsLoggingEnabled defaults to true, upgrading starts writing every audit entry, including its title and message, to ILogger and therefore to Application Insights. In some services those carry patient details such as NHS numbers, and every audit adds to telemetry volume and cost. If your service is not ready for that, set IsAuditAppInsightsLoggingEnabled to false before upgrading.\n\t\t\t- Each audit is logged once, at its own LogLevel, under the category NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics.Clients.Brokers.Loggings.LoggingBroker, with AuditType, Title, Message, AuditId, CorrelationId, UserId and CreatedDate as separate properties (custom dimensions in Application Insights). The host's logging filters must allow that category. The library takes no Application Insights dependency.\n\t\t\t- Storage is always written first. A failure to write to the logger never fails the call: it is logged as an error, and RecordAuditAsync and AddAuditAsync still return the stored entry.\n\t\t\t- With IsAuditDatabaseLoggingEnabled false, RecordAuditAsync and AddAuditAsync return the entry that would have been stored, without touching storage.\n\t\t\t- SecurityAuditRetentionPeriodInDays defaults to 730 rather than 30. The security audit purge is still off unless IsSecurityAuditPurgingAllowed is true.\n\t\t\t- Security audits are never written to the logger, and metrics are unchanged.\n\t\t\t- Depends on Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration.Abstractions, Configuration.Binder, DependencyInjection and Logging.Abstractions 10.0.13.\n\t\t\t- Upgrade guide: https://github.com/NHSISL/NHSOneLondon.AuditAndMetrics#upgrading-from-02x",
